    "innovation": "This paper develops a homoclimatic typology for the Brazilian Semi-Arid region by integrating meteorological data with sociodemographic indicators through cluster analysis, enabling a more precise characterization of the region\u2019s climatic zones and their relationship with population dynamics and vulnerabilities.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "IS_OF_TYPE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Drought",
            "target_entity_type": "NaturalHazardType",
            "paragraph": "The history of the Brazilian Semi-Arid (BSA) region is intrinsically linked to extreme climatic variations, such as prolonged droughts and increasing aridity, which severely impact water security, food security, and socioeconomic stability in the region.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Brazilian Semi-Arid region",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Global warming, characterized by an increase in the Earth's average temperature, has altered rainfall patterns in the Brazilian Semi-Arid (BSA) region, intensifying droughts and increasing water and food insecurity, especially in communities with low adaptive capacity (Barbosa, 2024; Guedes et al., 2024).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Brazil",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "The impacts of climate change, including the increased frequency of extreme events, tend to be more severe in tropical countries such as Brazil due to a combination of environmental, social, and economic vulnerabilities, which can result in significant consequences such as biodiversity loss and worsening social inequalities (Nobre et al., 2016; Rathore, 2024).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "BSA III",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The results revealed rising temperatures, intensifying droughts, and increased vulnerability in areas such as BSA III, characterized by severe aridity and limited infrastructure.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Brazilian Semi-Arid region",
            "source_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "relation": "HAS_CLIMATE_ZONE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Dry",
            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "The BSA has an average annual rainfall of 800 mm, higher than other semi-arid regions, but is characterized by marked temporal and spatial variability. In the North, rainfall is concentrated between March and May, with up to 310 mm, while in the South it occurs from December to February, with up to 389 mm (Marengo, 2020; Silva et al., 2023). This variability requires water management and agricultural planning strategies, given the climate vulnerability. Average temperatures range from 24 to 27\u00b0C, with precipitation concentrated in 3 to 4 months, resulting in a negative water balance and high aridity index (Souza et al., 2015; Mutti et al., 2020; Vieira et al., 2021).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "BSA III",
            "source_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "relation": "HAS_CLIMATE_ZONE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Dry",
            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "BSA III, defined by more arid conditions and greater water deficits, shows increased susceptibility to desertification.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "drought",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "BSA I",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The BSA comprises subregions with distinct characteristics. BSA I exhibits notable social advances but remains vulnerable to recurrent droughts; BSA II shows strong population growth associated with agricultural activities, yet is increasingly affected by declining rainfall; BSA III faces demographic constraints but has achieved improvements in human development indicators; and BSA IV is characterized by population decline and advanced aging.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
